KMS Existing Features

 



Feature / Use case

Description

Benefits

Centralized Management of Keys

Manages the entire lifecycle of cryptographic keys, from creation and distribution to archival and destruction, ensuring secure handling of keys throughout their lifecycle.

Centralized platform to manage the cryptographic keys for all needs.

Secure Key Transfer

Facilitates the transfer of keys between different systems/applications/departments, while ensuring keys are not compromised during the transfer process.

Enables users to securely share keys between servers, applications and departments in few clicks, without keeping any replica in the ecosystem.

Ensures security of all the keys being shared.

Tokenization (Vaultless and Vault-based): 

Supports both vault less and vault-based tokenization methods for securely replacing sensitive data with unique identification symbols that retain all the essential information without compromising its security.

It can be used to encrypt/mask sensitive data of all kinds.

BYOK (Bring Your Own Key)

Enables users to keep central repository or replica of all the keys already in use but not generated using KMS portal.

Provide platform to keep and track the status of all the keys already in use.

Azure BYOK

Allows you to bring and control your encryption keys within the Azure cloud, giving you complete control over data encryption.

Provides secure transaction and sharing of keys from Azure cloud to Bank with few clicks.

AWS BYOK

BYOK functionality to Amazon Web Services, enables secure key management within the AWS cloud environment.

Allows AOs to share the keys with AWS securely with few clicks

BYOE (Bring Your Own Encryption)

While it provides multiple algorithms for encryption but it also enables user to use own encryption mechanisms to protect data, providing greater control over the security of your information.

Provide flexibility to user to use their algorithm for encryption of data.

Role Based Access Control

Implements strict role-based access control, ensuring that only authorized personnel can access and manage cryptographic keys

Keys can be accessed by authorised users only.

 

 

